<title>USA: U.S. reviewing WTO report on EU banana row.</title>
<headline>U.S. reviewing WTO report on EU banana row.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky Friday said the U.S. was reviewing a World Trade Organization panel finding on the banana trade row with the European Union.</p>
<p>&quot;We are reviewing the report. It is very lengthy and very dense. We are reviewing it and are generally pleased,&quot; Barshefsky told reporters after speaking to a cattlemen's group.</p>
<p>Earlier this week, a WTO panel issued a preliminary ruling that the EU's banana import regime violated open trading rules, according to diplomats.</p>
<p>They said the report, issued after nearly 10 months of deliberations, recommended that the WTO's Dispute Settlement Body ask Brussels to bring the regime into line with its obligations under global trade accords.</p>
<p>The text of the report was not made public but was delivered to the EU and U.S. trade missions in Geneva and to the offices of four Latin American countries who had joined the U.S. in challenging Brussels on the issue.</p>
</text>
